1
00:00:07,438 --> 00:00:09,860
大家好，欢迎回到 showoffer.io。
Hey everyone, welcome back to showoffer.io.

2
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:13,900
今天我们要设计一个智能电网设备控制系统。
Today we are going to design a smart grid device control system.

3
00:00:14,734 --> 00:00:19,540
这个页面的副标题其实是对这个问题的最佳一句话描述。
The subtitle on this page is actually the best one-line description of this problem.

4
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:25,580
这是一个在不可靠边缘网络上的分布式闭环控制系统。
This is a distributed, closed-loop control system over an unreliable edge.

5
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:32,140
这个循环很简单：计划、指令、观测、调整。
The loop is simple to say, plan, command, observe, adjust.

6
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:37,200
但难点在于这些设备分布在公共互联网上。
But the hard part is that the devices live out on the public Internet.

7
00:00:38,158 --> 00:00:46,460
它们会掉线、重连、消息重复、遥测数据延迟，有时甚至直接拒绝指令。
They disappear, reconnect, duplicate messages, delay telemetry, and sometimes simply refuse the command.

8
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:56,840
所以，与其直接跳到巨大的架构图，我想按照我在 Unreal-InnerReal 中会做的方式来构建。
So instead of jumping straight into a giant architecture diagram, I want to build this way I would like to do in Unreal-InnerReal.

9
00:00:57,294 --> 00:01:06,480
我们将从产品循环开始，找出简单版本失效的地方，
并让每个失败案例迫使设计中加入相应的机制。
We'll start with the product loop, identify where the simple version
breaks, and let each failure case force one mechanism into the design.

10
00:01:07,918 --> 00:01:19,240
所以整个视频中需要记住的关键点是：平台永远无法获得完美的信息，
但它仍必须做出安全且可解释的决策。
So the key thing to keep in mind for this entire video is the platform never has the perfect information,
but it still has to make safe, explainable decisions.

11
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:25,280
现在让我们把产品，或者说系统，具体化。
So now let's make the product, or say the system, concrete.

12
00:01:26,478 --> 00:01:31,120
想象一下，一个电网运营商管理着一百万台联网设备。
Imagine a grid operator managed a million of the connected devices.

13
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:40,100
这些设备可能是 EV 充电桩、HVAC 系统、冰箱、工业设备，甚至是整栋建筑。
It could be the EV chargers, HVAC system, refrigerators, industrial equipment, and even the entire buildings.

14
00:01:41,358 --> 00:01:48,660
运营商会创建一个任务计划，比如「Northeast HVAC 在两小时内削减 20% 的电力」。
The operator creates a campaign like NorthEast HVAC cut power by 20% for two hours.

15
00:01:49,614 --> 00:01:52,640
观测结果，并在必要时进行调整。
Observe the result and adjust if necessary.

16
00:01:53,760 --> 00:02:01,460
在我们缩放后的车队中大约有 1000 万台设备，所有的通信都在公共互联网上进行。
There are roughly 10 million devices in our zoomed fleet and all communication happens over the public internet.

17
00:02:02,702 --> 00:02:05,080
这立刻给我们带来几个问题。
That immediately gives us several problems.

18
00:02:06,158 --> 00:02:08,919
当发出指令时，设备可能处于离线状态。
A device can be offline when the command is issued.

19
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:12,760
指令可能会被延迟或重复。
A command can be delayed or duplicated.

20
00:02:14,126 --> 00:02:15,880
设备所有者可能会拒绝。
The device owner may refuse.

21
00:02:17,006 --> 00:02:24,560
设备可能会确认指令，但实际上并没有减少电力负载。
The device can acknowledge the command but still does not approve the electrical load actually dropped.

22
00:02:25,646 --> 00:02:36,548
遥测数据可能会延迟到达、重复或乱序，而且在最初断电后，一百万台设备可能会几乎同时重连。
Telemetry can arrive late, duplicated, or out of order, and after original outage,
a million devices might reconnect at nearly the same time.

23
00:02:38,382 --> 00:02:43,580
所以我会明确告诉面试官：嘿，我现在正在设计这个仪表盘的监控。
So I would explicitly tell the interviewer, hey, I'm now designing a monitoring of this dashboard.

24
00:02:44,302 --> 00:02:47,000
监控是唯一的证据通道。
The monitoring is the only evidence channel.

25
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:55,060
实际的产品或系统是一个控制循环，它试图改变车队的行为并学习发生了什么。
The actual product or system is a control loop that tries to change the fleet behavior and learns what happened.

26
00:02:56,622 --> 00:03:01,660
这里一个有用的澄清是：下一次调整是手动还是自动的。
So useful clarification here is whether the next adjustment is a manual or automated.

27
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,180
对于这个设计来说，两种都可以。
Either is fine for this design.

28
00:03:04,782 --> 00:03:10,840
我们可以让人工操作员创建下一个任务计划，也可以由策略引擎来执行。
We can't let a human operator create the next campaign, or a policy engine can do it.

29
00:03:11,822 --> 00:03:14,520
分布式系统的要求基本是一样的。
The distributed system requirements are mostly the same.

30
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:18,860
下一步操作需要透明度，以及版本化的证据。
The next action needs transparency, versioned evidence.

31
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,020
现在
Now

32
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:28,280
在画框图之前，我先把我们的四个问题列在这页上。
before drawing the boxes, I would surface our four questions on this page.

33
00:03:29,262 --> 00:03:35,100
所以，在讨论系统的任何框架之前，这些实际上是针对整个系统的四个压力测试。
So they're really the four stress tests for the entire system before we're talking about any framing of the system.

34
00:03:36,206 --> 00:03:43,800
第一，ACK 证明了什么，又没证明什么？
Number one, what does an ACK prove or acknowledge prove and what does it not prove?

35
00:03:44,654 --> 00:03:47,340
也就是说，如果一个设备发送了 ACK 确认。
So if a device says ACK acknowledgement.

36
00:03:48,078 --> 00:03:57,100
那是否意味着消息送达了、指令被接受了、设定点变了，还是物理负载真的下降了？
Does that mean the message arrived, the command was accepted, the setpoint changed, or the physical load actually dropped?

37
00:03:57,646 --> 00:03:58,820
这些情况是不同的。
So those things are different.

38
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:08,480
第二，如果一个设备在较新的指令已经替换了它错过的指令后重新连接，会发生什么？
And number two, what if a device reconnects after a newer command has already replaced the one it missed?

39
00:04:09,998 --> 00:04:17,959
如果一个旧的减载指令在 restore 之后到达，我们可能会产生与预期物理行为完全相反的结果。
If an old reduced command arrives after a restore, we can create the exact opposite of the intended physical behavior.

40
00:04:19,918 --> 00:04:26,700
第三，如果一百万台设备同时重放两小时的遥测数据会怎样？
Number three, what if a million devices replay two hours of telemetry at once?

41
00:04:27,790 --> 00:04:29,740
这不仅仅是一个吞吐量问题。
This is not just a throughput question.

42
00:04:30,542 --> 00:04:37,800
历史积压可能会在操作员最需要当前状态的时候，遮蔽实时控制。
The historical backlog can blind the live control exactly when the operator needs the current stat most.

43
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:45,680
4. 如果延迟的数据证明早前的升级是不必要的，该怎么办？
4. What if the late data proves that an early escalation was unnecessary?

44
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:49,920
是我们覆盖历史记录，还是我们想保留两个版本？
Do we override the history or we want to keep both versions?

45
00:04:51,438 --> 00:04:57,580
我喜欢在架构设计前问这些问题，因为每个答案都会迫使我们在后期采用具体的机制。
I like asking this before architecture because each answer forces a concrete mechanism later.

46
00:04:58,190 --> 00:05:10,724
比如指令标识、排序和过期、分离实时和追赶路径、
事件时间处理、版本汇总，以及分离传输与物理评估。
The command identity, ordering and expiration, separate live and catch-up paths, event time processing, version roll-ups,
and separate transport versus the physical assessment.

47
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:17,780
这里有一个面试技巧：不要把这些当成琐碎的知识点来提问。
So here's one interview tip don't present this as a trivia questions.

48
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:23,060
要把它们作为你想与面试官确认的设计约束来呈现。
Present them as the design constraints you want to validate with the interviewer.

49
00:05:23,758 --> 00:05:29,820
如果面试官说，例如，指令永远不会过期，那么你的指令语义就会改变。
If the interviewer says, for example, commands never expire, then your command semantics change.

50
00:05:30,574 --> 00:05:34,680
所以澄清假设是系统设计面试的一部分。
So clarifying the assumptions is part of the design interview system.

51
00:05:38,350 --> 00:05:43,170
在最近的面试中，越来越多的公司开始在招聘流程中引入 AI 编程环节。
In recent interviews, more and more companies are introducing AI coding rounds into their hiring process.

52
00:05:43,822 --> 00:05:47,110
但 AI 编程不仅仅是让 AI 帮你写代码。
But AI coding isn't just about asking AI to write code for you.

53
00:05:47,790 --> 00:05:57,350
你有没有掉入常见的坑里，比如在不经过验证的情况下使用 AI 生成的代码，
或者在不理解或挑战 AI 方案的情况下盲目遵循它？
Have you ever fallen into common red flags like using AI-generated code without
verification or blindly following the AI solution without understanding or challenging it?

54
00:05:57,350 --> 00:06:06,730
无论你是否已经参加过 AI 编程面试，或者完全不知道该期待什么，
ShowOffer 有全新的 AI 编程面试指南来帮助你准备。
