ShowOffer has a new AI coding interview guide to help you prepare.

55
00:06:07,438 --> 00:06:17,170
你将了解到常见的 AI 编程环节类型、面试官如何评估你的表现、他们关注的关键维度，
最重要的是，如何进行有效的练习。
You will learn the common types of AI coding rounds, how interviewers evaluate your performance, the key dimensions they look for,
and most importantly, how to practice effectively.

56
00:06:18,158 --> 00:06:24,630
如果你想要实操经验，ShowOffer 还推出了专门的 AI 编程模拟面试和辅导课程。
And if you want hands-on experience, ShowOffer has also launched a dedicated AI coding mock interview and coaching sessions.

57
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:33,190
在真实的 AI 编程环境中与经验丰富的教练一起练
习，找出你的弱点，并在正式面试前提升你的表现。
Practice with experienced coaches in a realistic AI coding environment, identify your weakness,
and level up your performance before the real interview.

58
00:06:33,934 --> 00:06:38,490
不要在毫无准备的情况下参加你的第一次 AI 编程环节，通过 ShowOffer做好准备。
Don't walk into your first AI coding round unprepared, get ready with show offer.

59
00:06:41,294 --> 00:06:45,930
现在让我们进入需求部分，并把问题正式化。
Now let's come to the requirements part and formalize the problem.

60
00:06:46,638 --> 00:06:49,890
我打算故意把需求控制得很紧凑。
I'm going to keep the requirements intentionally tight.

61
00:06:50,730 --> 00:06:59,250
四个功能需求，四个非功能需求，一个规模估算，还有我们刚刚提到的四个后续问题。
Four functional requirements, four non-functional requirements, one scale estimate,
and then four follow-up questions we just introduced.

62
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:03,090
我们的目标不是列出所有可能的功能。
The goal is not to list every possible feature.

63
00:07:03,694 --> 00:07:08,750
而是定义最基础的契约，让后面的架构设计在逻辑上变得必要。
It is to define the minimum contract that makes the later architecture logically necessary.

64
00:07:12,350 --> 00:07:16,630
所以这里有四个功能需求，每一个都直接对应一个流程。
So there are four functional requirements, and each maps directly to one flow.

65
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:21,090
功能需求一是任务计划。
Functional requirement number one is campaign planning.

66
00:07:22,126 --> 00:07:28,910
用户定义目标组、操作功能、削减量、时间窗口和过期时间。
A user defines the target group, the action, function, the reduction amount, the time window, and expiration.

67
00:07:29,902 --> 00:07:34,010
我们先处理这个意图，然后再异步去执行。
We process that intent first, then find out asynchronously.

68
00:07:35,370 --> 00:07:38,470
功能需求二是发送指令。
Function requirement number two is sending the commands.

69
00:07:39,438 --> 00:07:41,710
在线设备应该快速收到指令。
Online devices should get a command quickly.

70
00:07:42,450 --> 00:07:46,910
离线设备只有在指令仍然有效的情况下，才能稍后收到。
Offline devices should get it later only if the command is still valid.

71
00:07:47,970 --> 00:07:49,450
重试必须是安全的。
Retries must be safe.

72
00:07:49,450 --> 00:07:55,310
过期的指令绝不能生效，且设备必须明确拒绝。
still commands must never take effect and the device must explicitly refused.

73
00:07:57,440 --> 00:08:00,800
功能需求三是反馈循环。
Functional requirement number three is the feedback loop.

74
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,960
也就是说，设备上报遥测数据。
So devices report telemetry.

75
00:08:05,038 --> 00:08:09,860
平台利用这些数据来回答更重要的问题：到底发生了什么。
The platform used this one to answer the more important question, what actually happened.

76
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:18,060
根据这些证据，我们可以维持当前计划、升级处理、放宽限制或执行 restore command。
From that evidence, we can hold the current plan, escalate, relax, or restore.

77
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:22,280
功能需求四是对账。
Functional requirement number four is reconciliation.

78
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:29,940
延迟样本属于它被测量的时间，而不是它恰好到达的时间。
A late sample belongs to the time when it was measured, not when it happened to arrive.

79
00:08:30,830 --> 00:08:38,220
所以延迟数据可以重新开启旧的评估窗口，更改结果，并发布修正版本。
So the late data can reopen an old assessment window, change the result, and publish a corrected version.

80
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:46,660
注意这个循环是如何闭合的：计划、指令、观测、对账，然后再次计划。
Notice how the loop closes the plan, command, observe, reconcile, and plan again.

81
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:55,280
所以我建议在面试中按照这个流程来说要求，而不是随意分组。
So one interview habit I recommend to say the requirements in this flow instead of grouping them randomly.

82
00:08:55,740 --> 00:09:05,040
这样一来，后面的高层设计就容易多了，因为你可以直接按功能需求一、二、三、四来谈。
So this makes the high-level design much easier later because you can literally talk with the functional requirement number one,
number two, number three, and then number four.

83
00:09:09,486 --> 00:09:16,100
现在来看这一页，这里有三个区别，能避免很多糟糕的设计。
And now let's come to this page which has three distinctions that prevent a lot of bad designs.

84
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:20,940
首先，指令送达不等于指令执行。
So first, command delivered is not command executed.

85
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:27,600
送达是传输层面的效果，而执行是设备侧面的效果。
Delivery is a transport effect and execution is a device side effect.

86
00:09:28,814 --> 00:09:33,540
第二，ACK，即确认，不等于物理验证。
Number two, ACK, acknowledgement, is not physical verification.

87
00:09:34,766 --> 00:09:38,420
设备可能会说“收到”，但功率曲线可能没变。
A device may say yes, but the power curve may not move.

88
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:48,020
可能是所有者覆盖了操作，也可能是本地安全限制生效了，或者指令已应用但物理系统反应缓慢。
Maybe the owner overrides it, maybe a local safety constraints wins,
maybe the command was applied, but the physical system reacts slowly.

89
00:09:49,582 --> 00:09:56,700
第三点极其重要：没有遥测数据等于未知。
And number three, and this is the one is extremely important, no telemetry equals unknown.

90
00:09:57,620 --> 00:10:01,840
沉默不代表成功，也不代表失败，它代表不确定性。
Silence is not success and it's not failure, it is uncertainty.

91
00:10:03,086 --> 00:10:10,580
所以我为什么这么在意这些区别，是因为如果你把它们混为一谈，你的下一个控制动作就会出错。
So why do I care so much about these distinctions, because if you collapse them, your next control action will be wrong.

92
00:10:11,214 --> 00:10:15,940
如果你把缺失的遥测数据视为成功，你可能会过早停止减载。
If you treat missing telemetry as success, you may stop shedding load too early.

93
00:10:16,718 --> 00:10:23,660
而如果你把缺失的遥测数据视为失败，你可能会过度修正，并向更多设备发送不必要的指令。
And if you treat missing telemetry as failure, you may over correct and send unnecessary commands to more devices.

94
00:10:25,102 --> 00:10:29,280
所以我也会快速把那些不在范围内的项目排除掉。
So I would also state out of the scope those items quickly.

95
00:10:30,126 --> 00:10:38,724
我们现在不解决电网物理学、需求预测、计费、设备固件内部逻辑或恶意遥测数据的问题。
We are now solving the grid physics, demand forecasting, billing, device firmware internals, or malicious telemetry.

96
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:45,060
这些都是正经问题，但它们会把面试话题从分布式系统的核心内容上带偏。
So those are legitimate problems, but they would pull the interview away from the distributed system core.

97
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:54,010
好了，聊完功能需求，我们来看看非功能需求。
All right, after talking about functional requirements, let's come to the non-functional ones.

98
00:10:54,798 --> 00:11:06,050
所以我会优先考虑另外四个方面：可靠性、延迟、可扩展性，以及正确性和不确定性。
So I would prioritize exactly another four, the reliability, the latency, scalability, and the correctness and the uncertainty.

99
00:11:07,758 --> 00:11:09,550
那我们先来看看可靠性。
So let's come to the reliability first.

100
00:11:10,638 --> 00:11:15,550
一旦我们接受了任务计划，服务崩溃就不应该让它消失。
Once we accept the campaign, a service crash cannot make it disappear.

101
00:11:16,270 --> 00:11:24,110
我们将使用至少一次交付和不重要的设备行为，而不是假装边缘网络能给我们提供精确的数据。
We will use at least once delivery and unimportant device behavior instead of pretending the edge network can give us exact ones.

102
00:11:25,230 --> 00:11:29,060
对于遥测数据，我们只在持久化写入后才确认。
For telemetry, we only acknowledge after a durable write.

103
00:11:31,246 --> 00:11:42,130
至于延迟，我们假设在线设备的 p95 指令交付在 10 秒以内，
并且初步的任务计划结果在几分钟内生效。
As for the latency, let's assume p95 command delivery under 10 seconds
for online devices and the provisional campaign result wins the minutes.

104
00:11:43,342 --> 00:11:47,130
这是一个物理控制系统，所以毫秒级并不重要。
This is a physical control system, so milliseconds are not at point.

105
00:11:48,110 --> 00:11:51,350
足够快到能影响下一个控制周期才是关键。
Being fast enough to influence the next control interval is.

106
00:11:53,550 --> 00:11:57,870
至于可扩展性，我们的研究状态已经很大了。
As for the scalability, our study state is already large.

107
00:11:58,894 --> 00:12:06,170
我们谈到了大约 1000 万注册设备，以及每秒大约 700,000 个遥测样本。
We talked about about 10 million registered devices and roughly 700,000 telemetry samples per second.

108
00:12:06,542 --> 00:12:10,430
所以真正的挑战是故障发生后的突发流量余量。
So the real challenge is burst headroom after the outages.

109
00:12:12,622 --> 00:12:16,610
而在正确性方面，这是很多面试深度所在的地方。
And in terms of the correctness, it is where a lot of interview depth lives.

110
00:12:17,350 --> 00:12:26,110
重复重试、保留事件时间、明确表示未知，并在延迟数据到达时修正历史记录。
Duplicate retries, preserve the event time, represent unknown explicitly, and revise history when the late data arrives.

111
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:32,140
现在，让我们进入技术细节部分。
And now, let's come to the skill parts.

112
00:12:33,518 --> 00:12:36,320
我们做一些足够的数学计算来支撑架构设计。
Let's do just enough math to drive the architecture.

113
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:42,620
假设有 1000 万注册设备，平均有 700 万在线。
So assume there are 10 million registered devices and 7 million online on average.

114
00:12:43,502 --> 00:12:47,720
每个在线设备每 10 秒发送一个遥测样本。
Each online device emits one telemetry sample every 10 seconds.

115
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:51,980
这大约给我们每秒 700,000 个样本。
that gives us roughly like 700,000 samples per second.

116
00:12:53,540 --> 00:13:07,620
例如，每个样本压缩后约为 200 字节，那么大约是每秒 140 兆字节，
或者在复制和其他开销之前，每天大约 12 太字节。
So at around 200 compressed bytes per sample, for example, that's about 140 megabytes per second,
or roughly 12 terabytes per day before replication and other overhead.

117
00:13:09,262 --> 00:13:12,100
现在来看一个有趣的数字：重连风暴。
Now an interesting number, a reconnect storm.

118
00:13:12,110 --> 00:13:20,080
假设 100 万台设备离线了 2 小时，每 10 秒产生一个样本。
Suppose 1 million devices were offline for 2 hours, and 1 sample every 10 seconds.

119
00:13:20,686 --> 00:13:23,820
每台设备缓存了 720 个样本。
Each device buffered 720 samples.

120
00:13:24,558 --> 00:13:30,360
那就是 7.2 亿个历史样本，在很短的时间内涌入。
That's 720 million historical samples, arriving over a short period of time.

121
00:13:31,460 --> 00:13:40,660
按每秒 700,000 的正常速率计算，这部分积压大约占稳态流量的 1700 万分之一。
At a normal 700,000 per second rate, that backlog represents about 17 millionths of the steady-state traffic.

122
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:46,600
但现在它们可能在短短几分钟内全部到达，而不是分布在当前的遥测数据中。
but now it may arrive in just a few minutes, not top of the current telemetry.

123
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:51,580
在绘制架构之前，这告诉了我们三件事。
That tells us three things before we draw the architecture.

124
00:13:52,398 --> 00:13:53,840
处理过程必须是异步的。
Processing must be asynchronous.

125
00:13:54,734 --> 00:14:04,420
我们需要在边缘和计算端之间建立分区持久化锁，而
且实时遥测数据不应该被强制排在历史数据追赶之后。
We need a partitioned durable lock between the edge and the compute, and
a live telemetry should not be forced to wait behind historical catch-up.

126
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:08,240
具体的数字在面试中可能会变。
The exact number can change in an interview.

127
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:12,900
这里重要的是利用这些估算来确定系统的形态。
what matters here is using the estimation to discover what system shape.

128
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:19,340
现在进入追问环节。
And now this is a follow-up question part.

129
00:14:19,854 --> 00:14:28,020
通常这些属于深度挖掘环节，但为了给你们做铺垫，这四个问题会提前出现。
Usually this falls into the deep dives but these four questions come up earlier here to give you some of the prelude.

130
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:34,540
所以第一个挑战，或者说第一个深度挖掘话题，可以是 stale commands（过期指令）。
So maybe the challenge number one or say the deep dive topic number one we can have is the still commands.

131
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:38,520
例如，如果 old reduce command 在 restore 之后到达。
For example, if an old reduce use arrives after restore.

132
00:14:39,118 --> 00:14:41,680
这主要是在测试可靠性语义。
That mostly tests the reliability semantics.

133
00:14:42,958 --> 00:14:45,880
第二个挑战是处理重连风暴。
The second challenge is going to be to reconnect the storm.

134
00:14:46,478 --> 00:14:53,880
如果一百万台设备上传两小时的历史数据，这必然会冲击你的处理能力和延迟隔离。
If a million devices upload two hours of history, that has to burst the handling and also your latency isolations.

135
00:14:55,420 --> 00:14:57,980
第三个挑战是延迟数据改变历史。
A third challenge is delayed data changing history.

136
00:14:58,990 --> 00:15:00,780
我们是基于缺失的数据进行升级的。
We escalated based on the missing data.

137
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:10,360
稍后，由于 Timing issues，许多设备已经 compiled（编译），
这种情况在测试正确性以及它们不完整的信息。
And later, Timing Tree approves many devices had already complied and that case test the correctness and their incomplete information.

138
00:15:11,854 --> 00:15:15,200
然后是还有 ACK 但没有物理效果的情况。
And then before is the ACK without physical effect.

139
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:19,480
也就是说传输成功了，但功率曲线没有变化。
So transport succeeded but the power curve didn't move.

140
00:15:20,014 --> 00:15:26,820
这实际上是在测试你是否将信息或消息状态与现实世界的证据分离开来。
That actually tested whether you are separate information or separate messaging state from the real-world evidence.

141
00:15:27,982 --> 00:15:34,040
所以当面试官问到这些问题时，不要直接跳到技术方案上。
So when an interviewer asks one of these questions, don't jump straight to a technology.

142
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:38,520
先从故障点出发，问问我到底需要什么样的保证？
Start with the failure and ask what guarantee do I actually need?

143
00:15:40,654 --> 00:15:42,030
这里有一个快速的展示笔记。
So there's a quick show-off note.

144
00:15:42,350 --> 00:15:45,570
这就是为什么实战模拟面试很有用的原因。
This is exactly why live mock interviews are useful.

145
00:15:46,170 --> 00:15:49,430
背诵使用 Kafka 或使用 MQTT 是很容易的。
Memorizing use Kafka or use MQTT is easy.

146
00:15:50,010 --> 00:16:01,890
难点在于当有人打断你，问如果 ACK 丢失了，或者设
备在 restore 后重连了，你还能否清晰地进行推理。
The hard part is having someone interrupt you with what if the ACK is lost or
what if the device reconnects after the restore and still reasoning clearly.

147
00:16:03,010 --> 00:16:13,950
ShowOffer 的教练在过去几年中帮助了数百名候选人，
包括准备 OpenAI 和 Anthropic 风格系统设计面试的人。
Our coaches from ShowOffer have worked with hundreds of candidates over the past years,
including people preparing for the open AI and anthropic style interview system design questions.

148
00:16:14,530 --> 00:16:17,490
而练习的核心就在于这种来回的互动。
And the practice is really about this back and forth.

149
00:16:21,774 --> 00:16:24,990
现在进入第二部分，核心思维。
Now let's come to the section number two, core thinking.

150
00:16:25,710 --> 00:16:29,670
我们发现这是整个视频结构中一个全新的部分。
We found this is a real new part of the whole video structure.

151
00:16:30,286 --> 00:16:35,410
原因是在讨论基础设施之前，我希望先讨论三个思维模型。
The reason is before the infrastructure, I want three mental model discussed in place.

152
00:16:36,238 --> 00:16:39,130
第一，这是一个闭环，而不是流水线。
Number one, this is a closed loop, it's not a pipeline.

153
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:45,970
第二，这是关于传输状态和物理结果，这是两个独立的维度。
Number two, this is about the transport state and the physical outcome, there are two separate dimensions.

154
00:16:46,890 --> 00:16:52,570
第三，即使信息不完整，系统也必须保持正确。
And number three, the system has to remain correct, even when the information is incomplete.

155
00:16:53,582 --> 00:16:58,370
所以一旦这些明确了，后面的设计决策就更容易解释了。
So once those are clear, the later design decisions become much easier to justify.

156
00:17:02,222 --> 00:17:03,204
让我们来看第一个。
Let's go to the first one.

157
00:17:03,850 --> 00:17:14,170
这里一个容易产生的想法是设备把数据写入消息日志、流处理器、时序数据库和仪表盘。
So the tempting picture here is devices writing into a message lock, a stream processor, a time series database, and a dashboard.

158
00:17:15,246 --> 00:17:21,190
那是一个完美的监控系统，但不是我们要设计的系统。
That is a perfectly fine monitoring system, but it's not the system we want to design.

159
00:17:22,089 --> 00:17:30,550
在这里，遥测数据不是最终部分，也不是最终产品，遥测数据是用来闭环的证据。
Here, telemetry is not the final part, or the final product, telemetry is evidence that closes the loop.

160
00:17:31,530 --> 00:17:35,570
所以真正的流程是从用户规划一个任务计划开始的。
So the real flow starts with a user planning a campaign.

161
00:17:36,526 --> 00:17:40,950
平台发送指令，设备做出反应，或者没反应。
The platform sends the commands, the devices react, or don't.

162
00:17:41,830 --> 00:17:51,810
它们产生遥测数据，平台评估结果并决定是否调整
计划，然后延迟的遥测数据可能会修正之前的结论。
They produce the telemetry, the platform evaluates the results and decides whether to adjust the plan,
then the late telemetry may revise an earlier conclusion.

163
00:17:52,878 --> 00:18:02,090
所以这个循环不仅仅是数据从左到右的流动，而是从行动到观测，到决策，再到行动。
So the loop is not just the data flowing from left to right, it is action to the observation to the decision to the action again.

164
00:18:03,110 --> 00:18:06,130
这个区别改变了我们需要持久化什么。
That distinction changes what we need to persist.

165
00:18:07,130 --> 00:18:17,510
监控流水线可能不在乎哪个任务计划针对哪个设备，指令是否过期，
或者哪个版本的证据导致了之后的决策。
A monitoring pipeline might not care which campaign targeted which device, whether the command expired,
or which evidence version caused a later decision.

166
00:18:18,478 --> 00:18:20,490
但控制系统绝对在乎这些。
But a control system absolutely does.

167
00:18:21,582 --> 00:18:27,550
所以如果面试官说下一个计划是手动操作，那也没关系，闭环是通过人类完成的。
So if the interviewer says the next plan is manual, that is fine, the loop closes through a human.

168
00:18:28,238 --> 00:18:32,650
如果是自动化的，策略引擎可以消费同样的汇总数据。
If it's automated, a policy engine can consume the same rollup.

169
00:18:33,614 --> 00:18:37,710
我会把策略逻辑与分布式系统的保证分开。
I will keep the policy logic separate from the distributed system guarantees.

170
00:18:38,542 --> 00:18:42,390
我们的工作是提供可靠的、带版本信息的证据。
Our job is to provide trustworthy, versioned evidence.

171
00:18:43,090 --> 00:18:46,890
具体的升级公式是可配置的业务逻辑。
The exact escalation formula is configurable business logic.

172
00:18:46,890 --> 00:18:47,850
然后
And

173
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:55,480
现在让我们来看看传输状态和物理结果。
now let's come to the transport state and the physical outcomes.

174
00:18:55,980 --> 00:18:57,240
这就是两个维度。
So these are the two dimensions.

175
00:18:57,934 --> 00:19:01,400
而这一页是整个架构中最重要的一页。
And this page is one of the most important in the stack.

176
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:06,800
左边，传输回答了消息发生了什么。
On the left, transport answers what happened to the message.

177
00:19:07,502 --> 00:19:08,644
我们送达了吗？
Did we deliver it?

178
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:11,440
设备确认了吗？
Did the device acknowledge?

179
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:13,840
它拒绝了吗？
Did it refuse?

180
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:14,880
它过期了吗？
Did it expire?

181
00:19:15,982 --> 00:19:18,140
最上方是评估答案。
And on the top, assessment answers.

182
00:19:18,958 --> 00:19:21,240
设备在物理上做了什么？
What did the device physically do?

183
00:19:21,998 --> 00:19:26,420
请求的结果是已验证、未验证还是未知？
Was the requested result verified, not verified, or unknown?

184
00:19:27,342 --> 00:19:29,540
所以这些维度是正交的。
So these dimensions are orthogonal.

185
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:33,380
设备可以处于「已确认且已验证」的状态。
A device can be acknowledged plus verified.

186
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:36,040
这是简单的情况。
This is the easy case.

187
00:19:36,942 --> 00:19:44,260
但也可能处于「已确认但未验证」，这意味着传输成功了，但功率并没有下降。
But it can also be acknowledged but not verified, which means transport succeeded but the power didn't drop.

188
00:19:45,454 --> 00:19:48,140
它也可以是「已确认但未知」。
It can also be acknowledged plus unknown.

189
00:19:48,980 --> 00:19:52,860
也就是说，设备确认了，但随后遥测数据消失了。
So the device acknowledged but then the telemetry disappeared.

190
00:19:54,574 --> 00:20:00,700
甚至一个被拒绝的指令，也可能恰好伴随着由于无关原因导致的负载下降。
And even a refused command could coincide with a load drop for unrelated reasons.

191
00:20:01,486 --> 00:20:04,440
这并不意味着是指令导致了减量。
That doesn't mean the command causes the reduction.

192
00:20:04,942 --> 00:20:10,180
它只是说明了为什么传输状态和观测到的物理现象是两种不同维度的真相。
It just shows why transport state and observed physics are different kinds of the truth.

193
00:20:11,598 --> 00:20:19,260
所以常见的错误是把它们当成一个巨大的生命周期，比如：待处理、已发送、已确认、成功。
So the common mistake is one giant life cycle like pending, sent, acknowledgement, success.

194
00:20:19,950 --> 00:20:23,460
「成功」这个词把通信和行为混为一谈了。
That word success fuses the communication with the behavioral.

195
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:29,240
所以这里好记的一句话是：ACK 证明了通信。
So the memorable sentence here is ACK proves a communication.

196
00:20:29,998 --> 00:20:33,260
遥测数据提供了物理行为的证据。
The telemetry provides the evidence of the physical behavioral.

197
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:42,320
第三点方法是：正确性必须在信息不完全的情况下依然成立。
And method number three, the correctness must survive in complete information.

198
00:20:43,590 --> 00:20:48,640
现在我们加入一个现实情况：平台在所有遥测数据可用之前就会采取行动。
Now we add the reality that the platform acts before all telemetry is available.

199
00:20:49,646 --> 00:20:50,560
这里有三个原则。
There are three principles.

200
00:20:51,438 --> 00:20:54,340
第一，让不确定性显性化。
Number one, make uncertainty explicit.

201
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:57,220
「未知」是一个合法的状态。
Unknown is a legitimate result.

202
00:20:58,020 --> 00:21:01,520
分别报告已确认的减量和不确定的减量。
Report confirmed reduction and uncertain reduction separately.

203
00:21:02,222 --> 00:21:06,212
让策略来决定它能有多保守。
Let the policy decide how conversative it could be.

204
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:10,080
第二，按事件时间处理。
And number two, process by the event time.

205
00:21:10,990 --> 00:21:18,760
例如，如果一个样本在 10:00:02 被测量，并在 10:10:00 被接收，它属于 10:00:02 的窗口。
If a sample was measured, for example, 10, 0, 2, and received at 10, 10, it belongs to the 10, 0, 2 window.

206
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:22,640
到达时间告诉我们后端是什么时候获知信息的。
Arrival time tells us when the backend learned something.

207
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:25,720
事件时间告诉我们现实是什么时候发生的。
Event time tells us when reality happened.

208
00:21:27,214 --> 00:21:30,980
第三，为每一个结论版本化，因为它们可能会变。
And number three, version every conclusion, that can change.

209
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:45,100
如果系统使用汇总版本 3 创建后续任务计划，而稍后到来的数据产生了版本 4，我们要保留两者，
否则我们就无法解释为什么之前做出了那个决定。
If the system creates a follow-up campaign using the rollup version 3, and the late data later produces version 4, keep both,
otherwise we lose the ability to explain why the earlier decision was made.

210
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:49,060
所以这为整个系统提供了一个很好的思维模型。
So this gives us a nice mental model for the whole system.

211
00:21:50,030 --> 00:21:54,900
指令采用至少一次交付，但受到实体、顺序和过期时间的保护。
Commands are at least once, but protected by the entity, order, and expiry.

212
00:21:55,880 --> 00:22:00,240
遥测数据是持久化的，它是分区处理的，并按事件时间进行处理。
Telemetry is durable, it is partitioned, and processed by the event time.

213
00:22:01,358 --> 00:22:03,960
而且所有的结果都是带版本号的。
And the whole results are versioned.

214
00:22:04,686 --> 00:22:10,160
随着新证据的出现，过去可以被重新解读，但未来只能向前推进。
The past can be interpreted as new evidence arrives, but the future only moves forward.

215
00:22:12,046 --> 00:22:14,000
所以最后这句话值得记住。
So the last sentence is worth remembering.

216
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:20,040
对账改变了我们对过去的认知，而下一个控制动作则改变了未来。
reconciliation changes our belief about the past, and the next control action changes the future.

217
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:26,160
现在让我们来看看设计决策以及每个决策背后的原因。
So let's come to the design decisions and the reason for each of them.

218
00:22:27,246 --> 00:22:31,220
这一页基本上就是决策形式的架构图。
And this page is basically the architecture in decision form.

219
00:22:32,014 --> 00:22:38,692
所以我们希望先持久化指令，并使用类似设备指令的东西来物化目标集。
So we want to persist the command first and use something like device command as a materialize the target set.

220
00:22:39,726 --> 00:22:40,080
为什么？
Why?

221
00:22:40,878 --> 00:22:44,520
API 返回速度快，并且可以在崩溃后恢复。
The API returns quickly and find out it can resume after a crash.

222
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:54,660
所以使用至少一次交付，再加上设备指令 ID、设备的序列号和过期日期。
So use at least once delivery plus the command ID, the sequence of the device, and the expiration date.

223
00:22:55,406 --> 00:22:55,680
为什么？
Why?

224
00:22:56,558 --> 00:23:00,240
我们不需要任何神奇的精确一次网络。
We don't need any magical exact once networking.

225
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:03,440
我们需要有效一次的物理行为。
We need effectively once physical behavioral.

226
00:23:05,102 --> 00:23:14,360
我们在边缘端将实时遥测数据和补齐遥测数据分开，然后在同一个持久化日志上进行汇聚。
And we do split the live telemetry and the catch-up telemetry at the edge, then converge them on one durable lock.

227
00:23:15,310 --> 00:23:15,620
为什么？
Why?

228
00:23:16,654 --> 00:23:22,404
重连风暴应该变成延迟而不是丢失，而且它不应该干扰实时循环。
A reconnect storm should become the lag not the loss and it should not blind the live loop.

229
00:23:23,700 --> 00:23:26,900
我们使用事件时间加上可见的水位线。
We use the event time plus the visible watermark.

230
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:27,800
为什么？
Why?

231
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:35,940
延迟样本必须落在现实发生的地方，而且消费者需要知道当前视图的新鲜程度。
The late samples must land where reality happens and consumers need to know how fresh the current view is.

232
00:23:37,614 --> 00:23:43,040
版本汇总和记录，例如基于汇总版本的后续任务计划。
The version rollups and record such as the based on the rollup version on the follow-up campaigns.

233
00:23:43,950 --> 00:23:44,300
为什么？
Why?

234
00:23:44,974 --> 00:23:48,460
我们需要最新的选择和决策时间选择。
We need both the latest choose and decision time choose.

235
00:23:49,774 --> 00:23:52,280
并且让控制具有自动过期属性。
And make the control self-expiring.

236
00:23:53,134 --> 00:23:54,300
这是安全属性。
This is the safety property.

237
00:23:54,894 --> 00:24:04,000
如果控制平面消失了，设备不应该永远停留在临时的减速状态，
去等待可能永远不会到来的 restore command。
If the control plane disappears, a device should not remain in a
temporary reduce state forever waiting for a restore that may never come.

238
00:24:05,102 --> 00:24:08,580
所以请注意，这些选择都不是从厂商产品开始的。
So notice that none of these choices start with a vendor product.

239
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:12,180
它们是从故障模式和要求的行为开始的。
They start with a failure mode and required behavior.

240
00:24:12,780 --> 00:24:19,380
这就是我希望在整个设计系统中达到的推理水平。
So that is the level of reasoning I would aim for into the whole design system.

241
00:24:21,774 --> 00:24:26,810
现在让我们进入第三部分，也就是实体和 API 设计。
So now let's come to the section number three which is entities and API designs.

242
00:24:27,918 --> 00:24:32,430
现在我们将定义能够表达我们四个流程的最简数据模型。
Now we will define the smallest data model that can express our four flows.

243
00:24:33,518 --> 00:24:43,310
目前我们只需要五个持久化的领域模型：设备、任务计划、设备指令、遥测样本和任务计划汇总。
We only need five durable domain models as of now, device, campaign, device command, telemetry sample, and the campaign rollup.

244
00:24:44,270 --> 00:24:46,450
然后我们将添加三种 API 形式。
Then we will add three API shapes.

245
00:24:47,170 --> 00:24:50,910
大部分有趣的工作都在这些 API 背后异步完成。
Most of the interesting work stays asynchronized behind those APIs.

246
00:24:54,380 --> 00:24:55,720
现在让我们来看看核心实体。
So now let's come to the core entities.

247
00:24:56,080 --> 00:24:58,200
让我们刻意保持模型简洁。
Let's keep the model intentionally small.

248
00:24:59,342 --> 00:25:02,540
让我们来看看这里的关系图。
Let's walk the relationship map here.

249
00:25:03,118 --> 00:25:04,820
首先是设备。
So device.

250
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:13,860
它是身份和目标元数据，包括设备 ID、区域、设备类别、优先级层级和退出选项。
It is the identity and the targeting metadata, the device ID, region, device class, priority tier, and opt-out.

251
00:25:14,862 --> 00:25:20,960
一个设备会发出许多遥测样本，并且随着时间的推移可以接收许多指令。
One device emits many telemetry samples and can receive many commands over time.

252
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:24,940
任务计划是用户的持久化意图。
Campaign is the user's durable intent.

253
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:38,800
它包含目标选择器、操作、参数、目标削减、生效跳过时间、过期时间，
以及可选的父任务计划链接和产生它的汇总版本。
It has the target selector, action, parameters, target reduction, effective skip time, expiry,
and optional links to a parent campaign and the roll-up version that cost it.

254
00:25:40,654 --> 00:25:44,720
设备指令是任务计划和设备之间的关联。
Device command is the join between a campaign and device.

255
00:25:45,800 --> 00:25:51,660
它的复合主键是任务计划 ID 加设备 ID。
Its composite primary key is the campaign ID plus the device ID.

256
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:59,040
这个角色意味着该设备，或者说这个设备，实际上是任务计划目标集的一部分。
That role means the device, or this device, was actually part of the campaign's target set.

257
00:26:01,070 --> 00:26:01,910
遥测样本。
Telemetry sample.

258
00:26:02,350 --> 00:26:06,570
它使用设备 ID 加样本序列作为复合键。
It uses the device ID plus the sample sequence as the composite key.

259
00:26:07,374 --> 00:26:10,596
序列提供了确定性的去重。
The sequence gives the deterministic deduplication.

260
00:26:11,214 --> 00:26:19,530
它存储事件时间和摄入时间、功率，以及可选的设备认为它正在执行的任务计划。
It stores both the event time and ingest time, power, and optionally the campaign that the device believes it is applying.

261
00:26:20,970 --> 00:26:22,990
最后一个是任务计划汇总。
The last one is the campaign roll-up.

262
00:26:23,470 --> 00:26:29,770
它使用任务计划 ID 加版本作为键，因为当延迟证据到达时，结果可能会发生变化。
It uses the campaign ID plus the version as its key because the result can change when late the evidence arrives.

263
00:26:31,530 --> 00:26:34,150
这里有几个存储方面的注意事项。
So here's a couple of storage notes.

264
00:26:34,990 --> 00:26:38,970
用户身份可以保留在权威系统中。
User identity can stay in the authoritative system.

265
00:26:39,910 --> 00:26:43,630
任务计划只需要通过用户 ID 创建它以供审计。
Campaign only needs to create it by the user ID for audit.

266
00:26:44,510 --> 00:26:47,670
呈现状态是热点、非正式的状态。
Presents is hot, informal state.

267
00:26:48,110 --> 00:26:53,250
所以我会把它保存在 TTL 缓存中，而不是把它变成另一个持久化的领域表。
So I would keep it in a TTL cache rather than turning it into another durable domain table.

268
00:26:54,446 --> 00:27:01,070
模型保持非常精简，因为每个表在我们的四个流程中都有直接的作用。
The model stays very small because each table has a direct role in one of our four flows.

269
00:27:05,870 --> 00:27:09,670
所以让我们谈谈任务计划和设备指令。
So let's talk about the campaign and the device command.

270
00:27:10,070 --> 00:27:12,964
一个是意图，然后是目标集。
One is intent and then is the target set.

271
00:27:14,478 --> 00:27:16,590
所以任务计划就是持久化的业务意图。
So campaign is the durable business intent.

272
00:27:17,870 --> 00:27:21,370
在我们联系设备之前，它必须先存在。
It must exist before we contact the devices.

273
00:27:22,702 --> 00:27:37,390
目标选择器可能包含 Northeast、HVC、Priority Tier
2 或更高，操作可能是减少百分比、cap 或 restore。
The target selector might stay, for example, Northeast, HVC, Priority Tier
2, or above, the action may be reduced percent, the cap bots, or restore.

274
00:27:38,550 --> 00:27:44,490
过期集特别重要，因为指令不能永远有效。
Expire set is especially important because the instruction must not remain valid forever.

275
00:27:45,998 --> 00:27:58,010
对于后续的任务计划，父任务ID告诉我们我们在响应什么，
而汇总版本告诉我们是哪个证据版本导致了这一决策。
And for the follow-up campaigns, parent campaign ID tells us what we're reacting to,
and based on roll-up version tells us which evidence version causes this decision.

276
00:27:59,250 --> 00:28:02,550
然后设备指令就把目标集 materialized 了。
Then the device command materializes the target set.

277
00:28:03,662 --> 00:28:10,230
复合键，即任务计划ID加上设备ID，锁定了最终时刻实际被目标化的对象。
The composite key, campaign ID plus the device ID freezes who was actually targeted at the final time.

278
00:28:10,990 --> 00:28:14,770
这很重要，因为集群成员身份之后可能会发生变化。
This matters because the fleet membership can change later.

279
00:28:16,398 --> 00:28:18,850
所以状态机故意设计得非常简单。
So the state machine is intentionally very small.

280
00:28:19,690 --> 00:28:25,030
包括待处理、已送达，然后是已确认或已拒绝。
Pending, then delivered, and then either acknowledged or refused.

281
00:28:25,902 --> 00:28:29,970
如果有效窗口先关闭，指令就过期了。
If the validity window closes first, the command expires.

282
00:28:31,430 --> 00:28:33,190
注意页面上的标注。
And notice the callout on the page.

283
00:28:33,590 --> 00:28:39,010
这里没有“已验证”，因为验证来自遥测数据。
There's no verified here because verification comes from the telemetry.

284
00:28:40,238 --> 00:28:53,970
所以在生产环境模式中，你甚至可以将响应状态与有效性分开，
这样一个已确认的账户稍后可能变为不再活跃，而不会抹除它之前已被确认的事实。
So in a production schema, you might even separate the responses state from the validity,
so an acknowledged account can later become a no longer active without erasing the fact that it was acknowledged previously.

285
00:28:53,970 --> 00:29:01,330
对于这次面试，只要你提前解释清楚语义，简化后的状态机就足够了。
And for this interview, the simplified state machine is enough as long as you explain the semantics earlier.

286
00:29:02,638 --> 00:29:09,050
所以关键教训是避免把传输、物理结果和策略全部塞进一个枚举值里。
So the key lesson to avoid stuffing the transport, physical outcome, and the policy into one enum.

287
00:29:12,430 --> 00:29:17,892
让我们谈谈遥测样本和任务计划，抱歉，是 campaign rollup。
Let's talk about the telemetry sample and campaign rollout, sorry campaign rollup.

288
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:22,560
所以遥测样本是可重放的证据。
So telemetry sample is the replayable evidence.

289
00:29:23,566 --> 00:29:27,900
所以要强调的两个字段是事件时间和摄入时间。
So the two fields to emphasize are event time and ingest time.

290
00:29:28,590 --> 00:29:30,580
事件时间驱动业务窗口。
Event time drives the business window.

291
00:29:31,120 --> 00:29:35,500
摄入时间帮助我们了解延迟和操作滞后。
Ingest time helps us understand the lateness and the operational lag.

292
00:29:37,070 --> 00:29:39,660
样本序列为我们提供了去重键。
Sample sequence gives us the dedupe key.

293
00:29:40,366 --> 00:29:49,480
如果设备因为丢失了 ACK 而重传同一个样本，我们可以接受至少一次摄入而不会重复计算。
If a device retraces the same sample because an ACK was lost, we can accept at least once ingestion without double counting.

294
00:29:50,900 --> 00:29:55,960
如果设备能报告它，那么已应用的任务计划ID对支持证据很有用。
An applied campaign ID is useful supporting the evidence if the device can report it.

295
00:29:56,718 --> 00:29:58,900
但我不会把它当作证据。
But I would not treat as a proof.

296
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:05,440
设备可以声称它应用了任务计划，但测得的功率仍显示没有减少。
A device can claim it applied a campaign while the measured power still shows no reduction.

297
00:30:07,930 --> 00:30:10,830
而 campaign rollup 是一个派生的版本视图。
And campaign rollup is a derived version view.

298
00:30:10,830 --> 00:30:25,030
它包含计数，比如已目标化、已验证、已拒绝、未知、
已实现的减少量、一定的潜在减少量，以及水位线。
It carries count like targeted, verified, refused, and unknown,
achieved reduction, a certain potential reduction, and also a watermark.

299
00:30:26,150 --> 00:30:29,348
所以这个页面上的简单例子是一个很重要的例子。
So the simple example on this page is an important one.

300
00:30:30,450 --> 00:30:34,190
假设版本 3 说确认了 30 兆瓦。
Let's say version 3 says 30 megawatts confirmed.

301
00:30:35,054 --> 00:30:36,750
延迟的遥测数据到达了。
Late telemetry arrives.

302
00:30:37,294 --> 00:30:41,070
版本 4 显示 37 megawatts confirmed。
Version 4 says 37 megabytes confirmed.

303
00:30:41,934 --> 00:30:42,590
所以两者都保留。
So both stay.

304
00:30:43,406 --> 00:30:43,870
为什么？
Why?

305
00:30:44,430 --> 00:30:47,870
因为可能已经基于版本 3 创建了后续的任务计划。
Because a follow-up campaign may have been created using the version 3.

306
00:30:48,210 --> 00:30:53,350
如果你覆盖了版本 3，历史决策看起来就会突然变得不合理。
If you override version 3, the historical decision suddenly looks irrational.

307
00:30:54,350 --> 00:30:58,050
所以我要在这里明确说明存储层级。
So I would state the storage hierarchy explicitly here.

308
00:30:58,450 --> 00:31:06,050
原始遥测数据是可重放的事实来源，但汇总数据是为快速决策优化的物化视图。
The raw telemetry is the replayable source of truth, but the rollup is a materialized view optimized for the fast decisions.

309
00:31:10,478 --> 00:31:15,830
在核心实体和数据模型之后，让我们来看看简化的 API 设计。
After the core entities and data models, let's come to the simplified API design.

310
00:31:16,430 --> 00:31:17,150
这里有三个调用。
There are three calls.

311
00:31:18,170 --> 00:31:25,210
API 接口可以保持非常精简，因为大部分复杂度都是异步处理的。
The API interface can stay very small because most complexity is asynchronous.

312
00:31:26,606 --> 00:31:33,690
针对功能需求 1，我们有带幂等性键的 post v1/campaigns。
For functional requirement number one, we have the post v1 slash campaigns with the item potency key.

313
00:31:33,690 --> 00:31:41,650
请求体包括目标选择器、操作、参数、目标减量、生效时间和过期时间。
The body includes a target selector, action, parameters, target reduction, effective time, and expiry.

314
00:31:42,950 --> 00:31:45,390
响应是 202 accepted。
The response is 202 accepted.

315
00:31:45,830 --> 00:31:51,130
一旦任务计划被持久化存储，我们就不会等待那五十万台设备。
Once the campaign is durably stored, we do not wait for half a million devices.

316
00:31:53,070 --> 00:31:59,550
至于功能需求 3 和 4，用户通过 get 请求读取最新结果。
And for functional requirement number three and number four, the user reads the latest result with a get request.

317
00:31:59,950 --> 00:32:06,970
例如，get v1/任务计划/任务计划 ID/rollup version number 等于最新。
For example, get v1 slash campaign slash campaign ID slash rollup version number equals to the latest.

318
00:32:08,366 --> 00:32:14,590
注意，版本、水位线和未知的减量瓦数都是契约的一部分。
So notice that the version, watermark, and the unknown reduction watts are part of the contract.

319
00:32:15,566 --> 00:32:19,590
我们是在展示不确定性和新鲜度，而不是隐藏它们。
We are exposing uncertainty and the freshness rather than hiding them.

320
00:32:21,230 --> 00:32:25,450
对于设备重连，我们在点位上有一个压缩的追赶批处理。
For reconnecting the devices, we have a compressed catch-up batch in point.

321
00:32:25,450 --> 00:32:31,550
设备上传许多遥测样本，我们仅在持久化追加后才确认。
the device uploads many telemetry samples, we acknowledge only after durable append.

322
00:32:32,270 --> 00:32:39,450
如果响应丢失，设备会安全地重试，设备 ID 加上样本序列可以去除重复数据。
If the response is lost, the device safely retries and the device ID plus sample sequence remove the duplicates.

323
00:32:42,030 --> 00:32:45,430
所以这套模式在所有三个 API 中都是一致的。
So the pattern is consistent across all the three APIs.

324
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:52,970
我们希望在边缘实现快速且幂等的写入，而在持久化边界之后处理昂贵或最终的工作。
We want a fast, idempotent writes at the edge, we want expensive or final work behind the durable boundaries.

325
00:32:53,710 --> 00:32:58,610
所以这个原则现在直接体现在下一部分，即高层设计中。
So that principle now show up directly in the next part, the high-level design.

326
00:33:03,086 --> 00:33:05,260
现在我们在这里构建架构。
Now we build the architecture here.

327
00:33:06,030 --> 00:33:11,540
对于高层设计的这一部分，我想让推理过程特别容易理解。
For this section of the high-level design, I want to make the reasoning especially easy to follow.

328
00:33:12,206 --> 00:33:14,920
我们不会先展示完整的系统。
We are not going to show the completed system first.

329
00:33:15,598 --> 00:33:19,020
相反，我们将从简单的业务循环开始。
But instead, we will start from the simple business loop.

330
00:33:19,502 --> 00:33:23,460
然后我们一个接一个地构建功能需求 1 到 4。
Then we build the functional requirement number one to number four, one by one.

331
00:33:23,460 --> 00:33:31,820
只有在每个流程都确定了各自的组件后，我们才会拉开视角，最后看完整的架构图。
Only after every flow has earned its components, we will zoom out and look at the full architecture as the conclusion.

332
00:33:32,660 --> 00:33:37,780
这样一来，在你看到最终架构图之前，每一个模块都有存在的理由。
And that way every box has a reason to exist before you see the final diagram.

333
00:33:41,294 --> 00:33:44,540
现在，让我们从最简单的产品流程开始。
Now let's start with the smallest possible product flow.

334
00:33:46,382 --> 00:33:55,000
所以在这里，我们可以看到从用户到任务计划，再到
设备、遥测数据、反馈，最后回到用户或策略的流程。
So here we can see from the user to the campaign to the device to telemetry, the feedback, and then back to the user or policy.

335
00:33:55,680 --> 00:34:05,520
在这个阶段，我故意不想在屏幕上出现 Kafka、MQTT、多个数据库或 20 种不同的设备。
At this point, I deliberately don't want Kafka, MQTT, multiple databases, or 20 different devices on the screen.

336
00:34:06,140 --> 00:34:09,500
我想问的是，这个简单的流程中哪些地方会出问题。
I want to ask what breaks in this simple flow.

337
00:34:10,600 --> 00:34:15,440
首先，如果设备在接受任务计划后立即崩溃了怎么办？
First, what if the device crashes right after accepting the campaign?

338
00:34:16,270 --> 00:34:21,480
那么用户的意图就需要一个持久化的存储，并且发现它需要具备可恢复性。
Then the user's intent needs a durable home and find out it needs to be resumable.

339
00:34:22,190 --> 00:34:24,480
这就成了我们的功能需求一。
That will become functional requirement number one.

340
00:34:25,838 --> 00:34:28,560
接下来，如果设备处于离线状态怎么办？
And next, what if the device is offline?

341
00:34:29,262 --> 00:34:34,739
那么确认信息就会丢失，而且旧的指令可能会在新的指令之后到达。
Then the acknowledgement is lost, and an old command arrives after a newer one.

342
00:34:35,630 --> 00:34:39,719
这迫使我们必须让指令交付变得持久化且重试安全。
That forces us to make command delivery durable and retry safe.

343
00:34:40,462 --> 00:34:42,679
这就是我们的功能需求二。
That becomes our functional requirement number two.

344
00:34:44,270 --> 00:34:49,920
然后，一旦指令到达设备，我们怎么知道它们真的生效了呢？
Then, once the commands are reaching devices, how do we know they actually worked?

345
00:34:50,862 --> 00:34:55,480
我们需要一条遥测路径，以及持久化的摄入和评估循环。
We need a telemetry path, durable ingestion and assessment loop.

346
00:34:56,110 --> 00:34:58,180
这就是我们的功能需求三。
That becomes our functional requirement number three.

347
00:34:59,342 --> 00:35:04,060
最后，如果用于评估的遥测数据延迟了 10 分钟才到达怎么办？
And finally, what if the telemetry for that assessment arrives 10 minutes late?

348
00:35:04,910 --> 00:35:10,160
那么我们需要事件时间处理，抱歉，需要事件时间处理和历史对账。
Then we need event timing, sorry, event time processing and historical reconciliation.

349
00:35:11,118 --> 00:35:13,040
这就是功能需求四。
That becomes functional requirement number four.

350
00:35:14,020 --> 00:35:23,400
所以，与其画出最终答案然后倒着解释，我们打算按照这些需求的顺序来构建架构。
So rather than drawing the final answer and explain it backwards, we are
going to grow the architecture in the same order as of these requirements.

351
00:35:24,440 --> 00:35:27,120
这是一个非常实用的面试技巧。
And this is a very useful interview technique.

352
00:35:27,660 --> 00:35:34,160
面试官可以清楚地看到是哪个故障或需求导致了每个新组件的出现。
The interviewer can see exactly which failure or requirement caused each new component to appear.

353
00:35:37,120 --> 00:35:40,900
好了，让我们从功能需求一开始，也就是任务计划。
All right, let's start with the function requirement number one, the campaign planning.

354
00:35:41,902 --> 00:35:44,180
我们的用户创建一个任务计划。
Our users create a campaign.

355
00:35:44,600 --> 00:35:49,920
比如「东北区 HVAC 功率降低 20%，从现在开始，2 小时后过期」。
Maybe NorthEastHVAC reduced 20% starting now, expiring in 2 hours.

356
00:35:51,040 --> 00:36:02,600
简单的实现方式是接收 POST /campaigns 请求，查询所有
匹配的设备，联系成千上万台设备，直到查完才返回结果。
The naive implementation would receive the post slash campaigns, query all matching devices, contact hundreds of thousands of them,
and only return when the find-out is finished.

357
00:36:03,662 --> 00:36:06,120
这会立即产生两个问题。
That creates two problems immediately.

358
00:36:07,086 --> 00:36:08,080
第一个是延迟。
The first one is latency.

359
00:36:08,910 --> 00:36:12,200
面向用户的请求时间现在取决于设备群体的规模。
User-facing request time now depends on the size of the fleet.

360
00:36:13,240 --> 00:36:17,200
第二个问题更严重，那就是模糊的故障。
The second problem is much worse, the ambiguous failures.

361
00:36:18,254 --> 00:36:23,800
假设我们联系了 200,000 台设备，然后设备崩溃了。
Suppose we contact 200,000 devices and then the device crashes.

362
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:26,080
任务计划被接受了吗？
Did the campaign get accepted?

363
00:36:26,798 --> 00:36:27,920
客户端应该重试吗？
Should the client retry?

364
00:36:28,462 --> 00:36:35,060
如果重试，是创建第二个任务计划，还是在相同的设备上重复目标？
If it retries, do we create a second campaign or double target it on the same devices.

365
00:36:37,166 --> 00:36:41,200
所以，我想要在这里有一个非常小且清晰的持久化边界。
So I want a very small, clear durability boundary here.

366
00:36:41,780 --> 00:36:45,480
首先，验证请求和 API 的幂等性键。
First, validate the request and API idempotency key.

367
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:49,080
其次，将任务计划写入持久化存储。
Second, write a campaign into a durable store.

368
00:36:49,820 --> 00:36:54,940
第三，一旦写入提交，就返回带有任务计划 ID 的 202 accepted。
And third, once the write commits, return 202 accepted with the campaign ID.

369
00:36:56,014 --> 00:37:00,260
只有在那之后，我们才异步解析目标设备。
Only after that do we resolve the target devices asynchronously.

370
00:37:01,230 --> 00:37:17,420
目标解析器查询设备注册表，例如，区域等于 Northeast，类别等于 HVAC，
符合条件的优先级层级，并排除退出的设备。
The target resolver queries the device registry, for example, region equals to NorthEast, class equals to HVAC,
eligible priority tiers, excluding the opted-out devices.

371
00:37:18,414 --> 00:37:26,120
然后，找出工作节点，创建一条设备指令，为每个选定的设备创建一条设备指令行。
Then, find out the workers, create one device command, one device command row per selected device.

372
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:28,800
这张表起到了重要的作用。
That table is doing something important.

373
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:31,100
它将目标集物化了。
it materialized the target set.

374
00:37:32,366 --> 00:37:42,140
例如，如果任务计划是 C1，设备 D7 存在，那么在任务计划启动时，D7 就是 C1 的一部分。
For example, if campaign, let's say C1 and the device D7 exists, then D7 was part of C1 when the campaign was launched.

375
00:37:42,860 --> 00:37:48,640
如果 D7 明天更改了区域，C1 的历史记录不会改变。
If D7 changes region tomorrow, the history of C1 does not change.

376
00:37:49,580 --> 00:37:54,980
这也给了我们准确的目标计数，并且是数据工作的自然单位。
That also gives us accurate targeted counts and a natural unit of the data work.

377
00:37:54,980 --> 00:38:01,520
而且因为键是任务计划 ID 加上设备 ID，所以它是重试安全的。
And because the key is campaign ID plus the device ID, find out it's retry safe.

378
00:38:02,300 --> 00:38:08,160
如果工作节点在执行过程中崩溃，它会重启，重复插入是无害的。
If a worker crashes halfway through, it restarts and duplicate inserts are harmless.

379
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:16,800
所以在功能需求一的最后，我们将用户请求转换成了持久化的每台设备的指令意图。
So at the end of the functional requirement number one, we have transformed a user request into a durable per-device command intent.

380
00:38:17,646 --> 00:38:19,780
我们还没有交付任何内容。
We have not delivered anything yet.

381
00:38:20,302 --> 00:38:21,260
那是下一个流程。
That is the next flow.

382
00:38:21,260 --> 00:38:22,080
所以
So

383
00:38:25,920 --> 00:38:28,580
现在进入功能需求二，指令交付。
now comes to the function requirement number two, the command delivery.

384
00:38:29,454 --> 00:38:34,660
现在，功能需求一已经给了我们持久化的设备指令工作。
Now, function requirement number one has given us the durable device command work.

385
00:38:35,360 --> 00:38:40,580
功能需求二要求，我们如何安全地将指令发送到不可靠的设备？
Function requirement two asks, how do we get a command to an unreliable device safely?

386
00:38:41,806 --> 00:38:47,100
我会将交付工作发布到持久化指令日志中，并以设备 ID 作为键。
I would publish the delivery work into a durable command log keyed by the device ID.

387
00:38:47,920 --> 00:38:55,080
以设备为键很有用，因为同一个物理设备的指令现在共享一个稳定的排序域。
So keying by device is useful because commands for one physical device now share a stable ordering domain.

388
00:38:56,174 --> 00:39:03,900
设备网关或 MQTT 代理（如果我们选择那是边缘协议的话）会消费这些消息。
A device gateway or an MQTT broker, if that's the edge protocol we choose, consumes those messages.

389
00:39:05,166 --> 00:39:08,040
如果设备在线，立即推送指令。
If the device is online, push the command immediately.

390
00:39:08,654 --> 00:39:14,240
如果设备离线，指令不能仅仅存在于一个网关的进程内存中。
If the device is offline, the command cannot just live in one gateway process memory.

391
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:27,000
它需要一个持久化发件箱或者由代理管理的持久化会话，指令会一直保存在那里，
直到设备重新连接或者指令失效为止。
it needs a durable outbox or a broker-managed persistent session and it stays
there until either the device reconnects or the command is no longer valid.

392
00:39:27,980 --> 00:39:36,640
所以具体的边缘协议可以是 MQTT，也可以是 WebSocket，或者任何双向的 gRPC。
So the exact edge protocol could be MQTT, could be WebSocket, could be any bi-directional gRPC.

393
00:39:37,680 --> 00:39:41,920
所以在面试过程中，我不会过度纠结于具体的名称。
So during the interview I won't over focus on the names.

394
00:39:42,478 --> 00:39:45,180
语义才是真正重要的。
The semantics are what really matters.

395
00:39:46,860 --> 00:39:52,820
因此，除了操作本身，每条指令还携带三个特别重要的视图。
So every command carries three specifically important views in addition to the action.

396
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:58,740
指令 ID 为逻辑指令提供了一个稳定的标识。
The command ID gives the logical command a stable identity.

397
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:04,780
设备序列为单个设备的指令提供了单调业务排序。
The device sequence gives the commands for one device a monotonic business ordering.

398
00:40:05,780 --> 00:40:10,000
过期时间告诉设备这条指令何时不再有效。
Expires at tells the device when this instruction is no longer valid.

399
00:40:11,086 --> 00:40:12,420
那么，我们为什么需要这三个要素呢？
So why do we need this 3?

400
00:40:13,966 --> 00:40:15,700
假设设备收到了一条指令。
Imagine the device receive a command.

401
00:40:16,430 --> 00:40:19,640
它执行了指令并发送了一个确认。
It executes it and sends an acknowledgment.

402
00:40:20,334 --> 00:40:21,760
但这个确认丢失了。
But the acknowledgment is lost.

403
00:40:22,542 --> 00:40:28,600
平台无法区分这种情况和指令本身丢失的情况，所以它必须重试。
The platform cannot tell that case apart from the command itself was lost, so it has to retry.

404
00:40:29,614 --> 00:40:31,800
这意味着重复数据是正常的。
That means duplicates are normal.

405
00:40:32,620 --> 00:40:38,180
如果设备已经处理过该指令 ID，它就不应该再次应用该操作。
If the device has already processed the command ID, it should not apply the fact again.

406
00:40:38,702 --> 00:40:40,660
它只需返回之前的响应即可。
It simply returns the previous response.

407
00:40:41,934 --> 00:40:49,140
如果一条指令的设备序列比已经接受的最新序列还要旧，它仍然应该被拒绝。
If a command has the device sequence older than the latest one already accepted, it is still and should be rejected.

408
00:40:50,510 --> 00:41:00,440
如果指令的 past expiration time 已过期，即使消息系统成功送达，也不应该执行。
If the command has the past experience site, it should not execute even if the messaging system successfully delivers it.

409
00:41:01,260 --> 00:41:07,580
否则，除非所有者或本地设备规则规定拒绝，否则就应用它。
So otherwise, apply it or refuse it if the owner or local device rules say no.

410
00:41:08,560 --> 00:41:22,680
所以我们的契约并不是完全依赖 at-least-once networking，而是 at-least-once transport，
再加上幂等性、排序和过期检查，这等于实现了重试安全的物理行为。
So our contract is not exactly one's networking, it is at least one's transport, plus idempotency, plus ordering, plus aspiring,
which equals to the retry-safe physical behavior.

411
00:41:23,566 --> 00:41:27,200
到这一步，我们可以可靠地要求 fleet 去做某些事情。
And at this point, we can reliably ask the flea to do something.

412
00:41:27,200 --> 00:41:31,740
但我们仍然不知道物理结果是否真的发生了。
But we still don't know whether the physical result actually happened.

413
00:41:32,526 --> 00:41:35,260
这就引出了第三个功能需求。
And that takes us to functional requirement number three.

414
00:41:39,342 --> 00:41:43,940
现在让我们来看看第三个功能需求，它涉及循环中的观测端。
So now let's come to the functional requirement number three, which has the observation side of the loop.

415
00:41:44,750 --> 00:41:48,390
设备会持续测量功耗。
So the device continuously measures the power usage.

416
00:41:49,390 --> 00:41:54,270
在连接状态下，它通过遥测网关发送实时样本。
While connected, it sends live samples through the telemetry gateway.

417
00:41:55,118 --> 00:41:59,150
在离线状态下，它将这些样本写入本地持久化缓冲区。
While online, it writes those samples to a local durable buffer.

418
00:41:59,150 --> 00:42:06,430
当它重新连接时，它可以例如通过追赶批处理API上传缓冲的历史数据。
When it reconnects, it can upload the buffered history through a catch-up batch API, for example.

419
00:42:07,278 --> 00:42:09,270
所以这些是不同的流量形态。
So those are different traffic shapes.

420
00:42:09,790 --> 00:42:13,910
它们最终都会追加到同一个持久化遥测锁中。
Both eventually append into the same durable telemetry lock.

421
00:42:14,730 --> 00:42:17,450
这个锁为我们提供了一个清晰的持久化边界。
That lock gives us a clean durability boundary.

422
00:42:18,382 --> 00:42:22,310
只有在遥测数据被安全追加后，我们才会确认它。
We acknowledge telemetry only after it's been safely appended.

423
00:42:23,470 --> 00:42:25,690
从这里开始，我们有多个消费者。
And from there, we have multiple consumers.

424
00:42:25,690 --> 00:42:34,230
一个消费者将原始遥测样本数据写入长期存储，以便我们稍后重放和回填。
One consumer writes raw telemetry sample data into a longer-term storage so we can replay and backfill later.

425
00:42:35,118 --> 00:42:37,510
另一个消费者是反馈处理器。
Another consumer is the feedback processor.

426
00:42:39,054 --> 00:42:43,570
现在我们终于可以回答 ACK 无法回答的问题了。
Now we can finally answer the question that an ACK could not answer.

427
00:42:44,210 --> 00:42:46,930
设备在物理上到底做了什么？
What did the device physically do?

428
00:42:48,334 --> 00:42:51,310
所以为了这次面试，我会刻意把评估逻辑简化。
So for this interview, I will keep the assessment deliberately simple.

429
00:42:51,950 --> 00:42:55,450
在任务计划开始前，获取一个具有代表性的功率基准。
Take a representative power baseline before the campaign.

430
00:42:55,982 --> 00:43:08,630
如果任务计划要求例如降低 20%，就推导出预期的功率水平，
然后从评估窗口内的遥测数据中计算出观测到的功率。
If the campaign requests a, for example, 20% reduction, derive an expected power level,
then calculate observed power from the telemetry in the assessment window.

431
00:43:09,326 --> 00:43:13,990
如果设备明确拒绝，结果就是拒绝。
If the device explicitly refused, the outcome is refused.

432
00:43:15,118 --> 00:43:18,710
如果遥测覆盖不足，结果就是未知。
If there is not enough telemetry coverage, it is unknown.

433
00:43:18,710 --> 00:43:27,630
如果观测到的使用量在一定容差范围内符合预期的降低，结果就是已验证。
If the observed usage meets expected reduction within some tolerance, it is verified.

434
00:43:28,398 --> 00:43:30,370
否则，就是未验证。
Otherwise, it is not verified.

435
00:43:31,630 --> 00:43:35,070
所以具体的基准算法是可替换的业务逻辑。
So the exact baseline algorithm is replaceable domain logic.

436
00:43:35,886 --> 00:43:43,524
它可以是最近的中位数、历史同时间的基准，或者是设备报告的设定点。
It could be a recent median, historical same-hour baseline, or a device-reported set point.

437
00:43:44,878 --> 00:43:47,570
分布式系统的核心点更重要。
The distributed system point is more important.

438
00:43:48,462 --> 00:43:53,060
评估是基于遥测证据的，并且是可重新计算的。
The assessment is based on the telemetry evidence and is re-computable.

439
00:43:54,450 --> 00:43:58,660
我们将这些评估汇总到任务计划的汇总中。
And we aggregate those assessments into a campaign roll-up.

440
00:43:59,270 --> 00:44:06,130
实现降低、未知的潜在降低，并根据结果进行计数。
Achieve the reduction, unknown potential reduction, and it counts by the outcome.

441
00:44:07,310 --> 00:44:13,550
现在用户或策略层就有了反馈，可以用来决定下一步该做什么。
Now the user or policy layer has feedback it can use to decide what to do next.

442
00:44:13,550 --> 00:44:20,910
如果所有遥测数据都能及时到达，我们就已经拥有了一个可重复使用的闭环。
If all of that telemetry arrived promptly, we would already have a reusable closed loop.

443
00:44:21,838 --> 00:44:25,650
但是，设备并不总是能及时上报。
But, devices don't always report promptly.

444
00:44:26,610 --> 00:44:31,830
所以，功能需求 4 要求处理证据延迟到达的情况。
So, the Function Requirement No. 4 asks what happens when the evidence comes late.

445
00:44:36,270 --> 00:44:42,450
现在我来处理经典的延迟数据案例，也就是我们的功能需求 4，对账部分。
And now I'll take the classic delayed data case, which is our Function Requirement No. 4, the reconciliation part.

446
00:44:43,330 --> 00:44:55,090
让我们看看，设备在 10.02 测量了一个功率样本，但因为它处于离线状态，
后端直到 10.10 才收到那个样本。
Let's see, device measures a power sample at 10.02, and because it's offline, the backend does not receive that sample until 10.10.

447
00:44:56,050 --> 00:45:03,490
我们做的第一件事是去重，使用设备 ID 加上样本序列，然后将其持久化追加。
The first thing we do is deduplicate is using the device ID plus the sample sequence and append it durably.

448
00:45:04,350 --> 00:45:11,070
然后我们必须回答关键问题：这条记录属于哪个评估窗口？
Then we have to answer the key question, which assessment window does this record belong to.

449
00:45:12,430 --> 00:45:17,230
它属于 10.0.2，因为那是物理测量发生的时间。
It belongs to 10.0.2, because that is when the physical measurement happened.

450
00:45:18,510 --> 00:45:29,130
所以，反馈处理器使用事件时间，而不是摄入时间，来找到原始的 10.0.0 到 10.0.5 窗口。
So, for the feedback processor uses the event time, not the ingest time, to find the original 10.0.0 to 10.0.5 window.

451
00:45:29,902 --> 00:45:36,170
如果那个窗口已经生成了结果，我们就重新打开它并重新计算受影响的证据。
If that window has already produced the result, we reopen it and re-compute affected evidence.

452
00:45:37,326 --> 00:45:53,570
假设任务 C1 之前有汇总版本 3，确认了 30 兆瓦，还有 8 兆瓦未知，
延迟数据证明实际上还有 7 兆瓦被削减了。
Suppose Campaign C1 previously had rollup version 3 with 30 MW confirmed and 8 MW unknown,
the late data proves that 7 more MW has actually been reduced.

453
00:45:54,798 --> 00:46:01,170
现在我们发布汇总版本 4，确认了 37 兆瓦，仅剩 1 兆瓦未知。
Now we publish rollup version 4 with 37 MW confirmed that only 1 MW unknown.

454
00:46:01,170 --> 00:46:03,870
关键在于，我们保留版本 3。
Crucially, we keep version 3.

455
00:46:04,718 --> 00:46:05,050
为什么？
Why?

456
00:46:05,742 --> 00:46:10,230
因为系统可能已经基于版本 3 创建了任务 C2。
Because maybe the system already created campaign C2 based on the version 3.

457
00:46:10,830 --> 00:46:17,810
所以 C2 可以存储父任务ID等于 C1，并且基于汇总版本号 3。
So C2 can store the parent campaign ID equals to C1 and based on the rollup version number 3.

458
00:46:18,830 --> 00:46:22,330
这样一来，在延迟数据到达后，我们保留了两个真相。
So after late data arrives, we preserve two truths.

459
00:46:23,310 --> 00:46:32,630
一个是我们现在认为实际发生的情况，由最新的汇总表示；
另一个是系统在做出早期决策时所知道的情况。
What we now believe actually happened, represented by the latest rollup, and what the system knew when it made the earlier decision.

460
00:46:33,774 --> 00:46:36,390
所以水位线让当前的完整性变得可见。
So watermark makes the current completeness visible.

461
00:46:37,454 --> 00:46:47,510
如果我们说墙上时钟是 1012，但水位线是 1006，消费者就知道更新的窗口仍然是初步的。
If we say a wall clock is 1012 but watermark is 1006, consumers know newer windows are still more provisional.

462
00:46:48,494 --> 00:46:52,790
这里的核心原则是，原始遥测数据只能作为证据。
And the core principle here is the raw telemetry is a can only evidence.

463
00:46:53,550 --> 00:46:57,490
任务汇总是基于证据推导出的版本化信念。
The campaign rollup is a version belief derived from the evidence.

464
00:46:58,550 --> 00:47:03,330
到目前为止，我们已经分别构建了全部四个功能需求。
And at this point, we have now built all four functional requirements individually.

465
00:47:04,398 --> 00:47:12,310
所以现在，只有现在，拉开视角看看这些碎片是如何构成一个完整系统的才是有意义的。
So now, and only now, it is useful to zoom out and see how those pieces form one complete system.

466
00:47:16,890 --> 00:47:23,790
好了，既然我们已经一个接一个地构建了每个功能
需求，现在让我们把所有内容整合到最终架构中。
All right, now that we've built each functional requirement one by one, let's put everything together into the final architecture.

467
00:47:23,790 --> 00:47:31,890
阅读这张图最简单的方法其实是按调用者顺序，遵循我们在整个设计中使用的相同顺序。
The easiest way to read the diagram is actually by the caller, following the same order we used throughout the design.

468
00:47:32,782 --> 00:47:37,010
让我们从橙色的功能需求 1 开始，也就是任务计划。
Let's start from the functional requirement number one in orange, the campaign planning.

469
00:47:38,030 --> 00:47:45,230
用户或策略层通过 POST API 调用 v1/campaigns 来创建一个任务。
The user, or the policy layer, creates a campaign through the post API call, v1 slash campaigns.

470
00:47:46,094 --> 00:47:52,070
第一个重要决策是，我们在进行任何大规模查找之前就持久化任务。
The first important decision is that we persist the campaign before doing any large find out.

471
00:47:52,078 --> 00:47:59,870
一旦这个意图被持久化，API 就可以快速返回，而不需要等待成千上万台设备。
Once that intent is durable, the API can return quickly instead of waiting for hundreds of thousands of devices.

472
00:48:01,486 --> 00:48:09,730
从那里开始，目标解析器读取设备注册表，并找出究竟哪些设备属于这个任务。
From there, the target resolver reads the device registry and figures out exactly which devices belong to this campaign.

473
00:48:10,650 --> 00:48:15,050
然后我们将那个结果持久化到设备指令记录中。
We then materialize that result into the device command records.

474
00:48:16,334 --> 00:48:19,990
这很重要，因为目标集现在是稳定的。
This is important because the target set is now stable.

475
00:48:19,990 --> 00:48:29,290
即使设备稍后更改了区域或资格，我们仍然确切知道哪些设备是被这个任务针对的。
Even if a device changes the region or eligibility later, we still know exactly which devices were targeted by this campaign.

476
00:48:30,638 --> 00:48:40,090
所以功能需求 1 基本上是将用户意图转换为持久化的任务，然后再转换为具体的每台设备工作。
So the function requirement number one essentially converts the user
intent to the durable campaign and then the concrete per-device work.

477
00:48:42,830 --> 00:48:48,100
接下来，沿着蓝色路径看功能需求 2，也就是指令交付。
Next, follow the blue path for the function requirement number two, which is the command delivery.

478
00:48:49,240 --> 00:49:00,680
这些设备指令记录被发布到指令日志中，然后由设备网关或 MQTT 层将它们交付给智能设备。
So those device command records are published into the command log, and
the device gateway or the MQTT layer delivers them to the smart devices.

479
00:49:01,998 --> 00:49:09,020
实际上，有些设备在线，有些设备离线，重试是不可避免的。
So, practically, some devices are online, some are offline, and retries are unavoidable.

480
00:49:09,020 --> 00:49:20,020
因此，与其试图在不可靠的网络上保证精确一次交付，
不如让每条指令都携带我们需要的安全重试语义。
So, rather than trying to guarantee exactly once delivery across an unreliable network,
every command carries the semantics we need for the safe retry.

481
00:49:20,686 --> 00:49:29,700
用于去重的命令 ID，用于排序的设备序列，以及过期时间，这样过时的命令就无法在之后执行了。
The command ID for the deduplication, the device sequence for the ordering,
and expires at two so that the stale commands cannot execute later.

482
00:49:30,830 --> 00:49:38,620
通过这种方式，功能需求二就实现了持久化的至少一次交付，
并能有效达到 at-least-once physical behavior。
So in this way, the function requirement number two gives us the durable,
at least once delivery with effectively one's physical behavior.

483
00:49:40,790 --> 00:49:45,444
现在来看绿色部分，也就是功能需求三，反馈循环。
And now come to the green pad, which is functional requirement number three, the feedback loop.

484
00:49:46,638 --> 00:49:53,710
设备接收到命令后，我们仍然不能假设请求的物理行为已经发生了。
Once devices receive the commands, we still cannot assume the requested physical behavior happened.

485
00:49:54,790 --> 00:49:57,510
设备会持续产生遥测数据。
Devices continuously produce the telemetry.

486
00:49:58,766 --> 00:50:09,090
当前数据通过实时遥测路径传输，而从故障中恢复的
设备可以通过追赶批处理 API 上传缓冲历史数据。
So current data goes through the live telemetry paths while devices recovering
from an outage can upload a buffer history through the catch-up batch API.

487
00:50:10,094 --> 00:50:13,670
这两条路径最终都会汇聚到遥测日志中。
So both paths converge on the telemetry log.

488
00:50:15,086 --> 00:50:22,290
从那里开始，我们保留原始遥测数据用于重放，而反馈处理器负责评估实际发生了什么。
And from there, we keep raw telemetry for replay and the feedback processor evaluates what actually happened.

489
00:50:23,502 --> 00:50:29,550
该处理器可能会将结果分类为已验证、未验证或未知。
That processor may classify the results as verified, not verified, or unknown.

490
00:50:30,542 --> 00:50:34,830
这就是我们之前讨论的区别变得至关重要的地方。
And this is where the distinction we discussed earlier becomes the critical parts.

491
00:50:34,830 --> 00:50:39,108
确认信息告诉我们通信发生了。
The acknowledgement tells us that communication happened.

492
00:50:40,238 --> 00:50:43,230
遥测数据为我们提供了物理行为的证据。
The telemetry gives us the evidence of the physical behavior.

493
00:50:44,270 --> 00:50:48,030
结果会被汇总到任务计划汇总中。
And the result is aggregated into the campaign roll-up.

494
00:50:50,180 --> 00:50:55,020
最后，紫色标注代表功能需求四，即对账。
And finally, the purple annotation represents the function requirement number 4, which is the reconciliation.

495
00:50:56,700 --> 00:50:59,300
遥测数据并不总是准时到达。
Telemetry does not always arrive on time.

496
00:51:00,334 --> 00:51:07,140
如果样本延迟到达，我们使用事件时间重新打开该测量值所属的历史窗口。
If a sample arrives late, we use the event time to reopen the historical window where that measurement actually belongs to.

497
00:51:08,302 --> 00:51:09,760
这可能会改变任务计划的结果。
This may change the campaign result.

498
00:51:10,480 --> 00:51:16,340
因此，我们不是覆盖之前的答案，而是将版本 N 发布为版本 N 加一。
So instead of overriding the previous answer, we publish version N to version N plus one.

499
00:51:17,582 --> 00:51:23,660
我们还会提供一个水位线，让消费者了解当前结果的完整程度。
And we also expose a watermark so consumers understand how complete the current result is.

500
00:51:24,814 --> 00:51:29,640
这就是为什么我喜欢把系统看作：原始遥测数据是证据。
And this is why I like to think about the system as the raw telemetry is evidence.

501
00:51:30,126 --> 00:51:33,360
汇总是我们基于这些证据得出的当前结论。
The rollup is our current belief based on that evidence.

502
00:51:34,574 --> 00:51:37,700
随着更多证据的到达，我们的结论可能会改变。
And as more evidence arrives, our belief can change.

503
00:51:40,270 --> 00:51:45,060
所以如果我们现在把视野放大，整个系统就是一个我们提到的闭环。
So if we now zoom out, the complete system is one closed loop as we mentioned.

504
00:51:45,560 --> 00:51:50,300
计划、指令、观测、对账、调整下一个计划。
Plan, command, observe, reconcile, adjust the next plan.

505
00:51:51,470 --> 00:51:55,960
用户创建一个任务计划，我们将其持久化，并解析设备集。
The user creates a campaign, we persist it, and resolve the device set.

506
00:51:56,814 --> 00:51:59,204
这些命令被安全地交付给整个设备群。
And those commands are delivered safely to the fleet.

507
00:52:00,206 --> 00:52:13,700
遥测数据从设备传回，我们评估物理结果，延迟数据可以修正该结果，
最后用户或策略引擎读取最新的汇总并决定下一步操作，形成一个循环。
The telemetry comes back from the devices, we evaluate the physical results, the late data can revise that result,
and finally the user or the policy engine reads the latest rollup and decides what to do next as a loop.

508
00:52:14,798 --> 00:52:20,560
至此，高层设计就完成了，这也完成了本视频的第一部分。
So that completes the high-level design and it also wraps up our part one of this video.

509
00:52:21,742 --> 00:52:33,460
到目前为止，我们主要关注如何构建正常的系统流程，
但当我们开始尝试破坏它时，架构会变得更有趣。
So far we mostly focused on how to build a normal system flow, but the
architecture becomes much more interesting when we start trying to break it.

510
00:52:34,382 --> 00:52:37,620
这正是我们将在第二部分中涵盖的内容。
And that's exactly what we'll do or we will cover in the part two.

511
00:52:38,670 --> 00:52:41,740
接下来，我们将深入探讨四个故障场景。
So we'll go through our four deeper failure scenarios.

512
00:52:42,320 --> 00:52:51,340
首先，如果设备离线，且在较新的 restore 命令之后收到旧的 reduce 命令，会发生什么？
First, what happens if a device is offline and an old reduce command arrives after a newer restore command?

513
00:52:52,718 --> 00:53:01,340
第二，当一百万台设备同时重新连接，并开始回传数小时的缓存遥测数据时，会发生什么？
Second, what happens when a million devices reconnect at the same time and start playing hours of the buffer telemetry?

514
00:53:02,702 --> 00:53:13,680
第三，如果缺失的遥测数据导致我们发布了新的任务计划，
但随后到来的延迟数据证明原始设备已经 compiled 了，该怎么办？
And third, what happens when missing telemetry causes us to issue another campaign,
but the late data later proves that the original devices had already complied?

515
00:53:15,118 --> 00:53:22,680
最后，如果设备发送了确认信息，但实际耗电量并没有下降，会发生什么？
And finally, what happens when a device says acknowledgement, but the actual power usage never drops?

516
00:53:24,014 --> 00:53:38,500
这四个案例将迫使我们深入探讨幂等性、排序、过期处
理、背压、事件时间和水位线、版本状态以及物理验证。
So those four cases will force us to go much deeper into idempotency, ordering, expiration, backpressure, event time and watermarks,
the version state, and the physical verification.

517
00:53:39,982 --> 00:53:42,916
所以，这个最终架构仅仅是个起点。
So this final architecture is just the starting point.

518
00:53:43,918 --> 00:53:49,320
在下一集，我们将对背后的每一个重要假设进行压力测试。
And in the next episode, we will stress test every important assumption behind it.

519
00:53:50,158 --> 00:53:51,940
请继续关注第二部分。
Stay tuned for part 2.

